1.4 "Project Marks" means the NexHaat name, logos, symbols, product names,
brand identity, and other marks, but only to the extent owned or controlled by
the relevant rights holder.

1.5 "You" or "User" means a person or legal entity that accesses, receives,
views, downloads, or seeks to use Covered Materials.

1.6 "Written Permission" means prior, explicit permission in a durable
written record issued by the relevant rights holder or an authorized
representative. It must identify the materials, permitted acts, purpose,
territory, duration, recipients, distribution method, and conditions. A
request, discussion, repository view, issue comment, silence, non-response,
public availability, or assumption is not Written Permission.

1.7 "Commercial Use" includes use for payment, revenue, advertising, resale,
subscription, client work, paid implementation, commercial advantage,
white-labeling, hosted services, SaaS, or inclusion in a paid product, to the
extent such use exercises rights controlled by the Licensor.

1.8 "Derivative Work" means an adaptation or other derivative material based
on protected expression in Covered Materials, as recognized by applicable law.

1.9 "Applicable Law" means mandatory laws, regulations, binding court orders,
and enforceable legal requirements applicable to the relevant person,
conduct, work, territory, and dispute.

1.10 "Third-Party Materials" means software, libraries, SDKs, frameworks,
fonts, icons, images, datasets, content, APIs, services, and other material
owned or licensed by a person other than the Licensor.

